{%- comment -%}
  PDP recommendations — candidate index (Section Rendering API only; no presets,
  so it never appears in the theme editor).

  Rendered on a collection URL with a price filter, e.g.
    /collections/yellow-sapphire?section_id=pdp-recs-index
      &filter.v.price.gte=14625&filter.v.price.lte=17875&sort_by=price-ascending
  (or /collections/all?filter.p.m.custom.gem_type=Coral&... for gems that
  have no collection of their own).

  Liquid can only iterate the first 50 products of a collection, so the PDP
  (sections/main-product.liquid) asks for narrow price bands sorted so the
  closest prices come first, ranks the pool by carat + price proximity in the
  browser, then renders the winners through sections/pdp-rec-card.liquid.
  Output is a compact JSON list: id, handle, price (paise), carats, whether the
  title marks it as a strand, and availability.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- paginate collection.products by 50 -%}
<script type="application/json" data-pdp-recs-index>[
{%- for p in collection.products -%}
  {%- assign _t = p.title | downcase -%}
  {%- assign _strand = false -%}
  {%- if _t contains 'strand' -%}{%- assign _strand = true -%}{%- endif -%}
  {"id":{{ p.id }},"handle":{{ p.handle | json }},"price":{{ p.price }},"carats":{{ p.metafields.custom.weight_carats | default: 0 | plus: 0.0 }},"strand":{{ _strand }},"available":{{ p.available }}}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
{%- endfor -%}
]</script>
{%- endpaginate -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "PDP recommendations index"
}
{% endschema %}
